# SEO on every page change

Public routes need unique title, description, and a **per-page** canonical. Never set a homepage canonical on the root layout.

- Helpers live in `src/lib/seo.ts` (`getSiteUrl`, `noIndexRobots`, `spotPageTitle`, JSON-LD builders).
- Index: `/`, `/about`, `/regions`, `/regions/[slug]`, `/guides/jerusalem-sunset`, `/guides/north-golan-sunset`, and `/spots/[id]`. Noindex: `/login`, `/spots/new`, `/spots/mine`, `/spots/[id]/edit`, `/admin`, `/auth/*`, `/api/*`. Pending spot suggestions are not public URLs. `/50` permanently redirects to `/about` and is not a separate URL. `/regions/judea-samaria` permanently redirects to `/regions` and is not in the sitemap. Region pages come from `SUNSET_REGIONS` in `src/lib/regions.ts`. The `/regions` index is `REGIONS_INDEX`.
- New public URLs go in `sitemap.ts` (via `listSpots()`, not `/api/spots`) and must not be `disallow`ed in `robots.ts`.
- Map lists that are virtualized in the client still need server-rendered links (`HomeSpotIndex`).
- Spot pages keep an `h1` and `spotJsonLd`. JSON-LD only through `JsonLd`.
- Spot `og:image` / `twitter:image` use the cover photo when it is public https. Spots without one use the home page card at `/opengraph-image` (1200×630), not a generated per-spot image. Twitter card is `summary_large_image`.
- `/regions` needs its own `opengraph-image.tsx` and `twitter-image.tsx`. A page-level `openGraph` object does not inherit the root card.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD - inherited by every route
export const metadata = { alternates: { canonical: "https://after-the-sun.com" } };

// ✅ GOOD - homepage only
export const metadata = { alternates: { canonical: "/" } };
```
